WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:38.038 --> 00:39.957
[♪ surreal music playing]

00:41.375 --> 00:42.417
[click echoes]

00:43.418 --> 00:45.212
[whooshing]

00:45.295 --> 00:46.463
[explosion]

00:49.383 --> 00:51.051
[high-pitched ringing]

00:51.134 --> 00:53.387
[Haran] Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.

00:53.470 --> 00:56.556
But that made me want
to get on a plane to go see you.

00:59.977 --> 01:01.103
Chan.

01:01.186 --> 01:04.481
-[EKG beeping]
-[♪ dramatic music playing]

01:06.316 --> 01:07.359
I love you.

01:13.865 --> 01:14.992
I love you, Chan.

01:17.619 --> 01:19.871
[EKG beeping continuing]

01:33.802 --> 01:34.845
[music fades]

01:34.928 --> 01:37.139
-[dripping]
-[ventilator hisses]

01:37.222 --> 01:38.974
[breathing heavily]

01:45.814 --> 01:47.316
[♪ dramatic music continuing]

01:49.276 --> 01:52.154
EPISODE 2

01:52.237 --> 01:55.282
[doctor] The accident in the US
happened last summer, right?

01:56.158 --> 02:00.537
It has already been three months
since you came to Korea for treatment.

02:01.705 --> 02:04.249
Have you recalled any more memories
after our last session?

02:04.833 --> 02:05.876
No.

02:08.086 --> 02:09.671
I just keep

02:10.589 --> 02:12.090
remembering one person.

02:13.300 --> 02:16.345
I keep remembering
how she called my name and woke me.

02:16.428 --> 02:18.430
[♪ dramatic music continuing]

02:19.806 --> 02:22.934
But no matter how much I try to remember,

02:23.018 --> 02:25.687
I can't recall who she is
or why I'm remembering her.

02:25.771 --> 02:26.980
[sighs]

02:27.064 --> 02:31.234
[doctor] Do you get images of her
in certain situations?

02:31.943 --> 02:34.196
[Chan] No, she's always just there.

02:35.280 --> 02:37.824
She's buried in my brain,

02:39.951 --> 02:41.536
just like that shrapnel.

02:42.120 --> 02:44.581
[doctor] Could it be someone you met

02:44.665 --> 02:48.001
during that year before the accident,
back when everything's a blur for you?

02:48.085 --> 02:51.463
[Chan sighs] I've always been alone.

02:52.798 --> 02:55.842
There can't be anyone
who says they love me.

02:55.926 --> 02:56.927
[grip tightens]

02:57.803 --> 02:58.804
[sighs]

03:01.348 --> 03:03.141
I'm not even sure if she exists,

03:03.892 --> 03:05.644
or if it's an illusion in my head.

03:06.269 --> 03:07.437
Or…

03:07.938 --> 03:09.439
if I'm just crazy.

03:10.482 --> 03:11.775
I wouldn't feel

03:12.693 --> 03:15.779
so frustrated if I at least knew that.

03:16.738 --> 03:20.575
[doctor] What kind of person
does she feel like to you?

03:22.911 --> 03:24.830
[Chan] Someone I have to meet…

03:28.166 --> 03:30.961
[♪ music intensifies]

03:33.338 --> 03:36.007
Sir, I'll just get off here.

03:36.091 --> 03:37.717
[lively chatter]

03:39.302 --> 03:40.762
[♪ sentimental song playing]

03:40.846 --> 03:44.182
[Chan] Someone who brought me back to life

03:45.350 --> 03:50.021
and seems to hold the keys to my life.

03:55.360 --> 03:58.613
[♪ sentimental song continuing]

04:17.549 --> 04:19.092
[panting]

04:40.238 --> 04:41.448
[fireworks whistle, exploding]

04:42.324 --> 04:43.325
[song stops]

04:44.743 --> 04:45.827
[explosion]

04:45.911 --> 04:47.954
[people exclaiming]

04:51.291 --> 04:53.001
[fireworks crackle]

04:55.003 --> 04:56.421
[footstep echoes]

04:57.088 --> 05:00.300
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

05:00.383 --> 05:02.469
[Haran vocalizing tune]

05:04.095 --> 05:05.138
[Haran] Try listening to it.

05:05.222 --> 05:06.556
I saw a vapor trail earlier.

05:06.640 --> 05:07.641
Chan.

05:07.724 --> 05:09.309
[Haran vocalizing tune on speaker phone]

05:09.392 --> 05:11.061
Hold on. Let me start over.

05:11.144 --> 05:12.646
Try listening to it.

05:12.729 --> 05:14.189
Hey, engineering student.

05:14.940 --> 05:15.941
Chan.

05:16.024 --> 05:17.150
Hey, Chan!

05:19.069 --> 05:21.071
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

05:21.154 --> 05:23.073
[panting] Hey. Sorry, Haran.

05:24.449 --> 05:26.201
Oh, that song?

05:27.244 --> 05:28.245
Sure. Send it to me.

05:28.328 --> 05:30.205
I'll listen to it.

05:30.288 --> 05:32.374
[high-pitched ringing]

05:32.457 --> 05:34.376
[fireworks exploding]

05:34.459 --> 05:35.585
[laptop pings]

05:36.336 --> 05:37.462
[laptop pings]

05:38.463 --> 05:40.090
[Hyeokchan sighs] I have to go in a hurry.

05:40.173 --> 05:43.093
Can you message her back
and say I have to go to the lab?

05:43.176 --> 05:45.178
Sorry. Do me a solid.

05:47.097 --> 05:48.223
Tsk.

05:48.306 --> 05:49.307
-[door closes]
-[sighs]

05:49.391 --> 05:50.767
-[laptop pings]
-Tsk.

05:52.686 --> 05:54.437
-[sighs]
-[laptop pings]

06:01.862 --> 06:04.155
[Chan sighs]
Sorry, I'm heading to the lab.

06:06.616 --> 06:07.951
[Haran] I was feeling trapped.

06:08.034 --> 06:11.037
I feel like I'm surrounded by walls today.

06:11.121 --> 06:14.416
I just messaged you
because I wanted to talk to someone.

06:14.499 --> 06:17.419
-But you're busy. Sorry I bothered you.
-[sighs]

06:18.128 --> 06:20.130
"Surrounded by walls"?

06:20.797 --> 06:23.174
I FEEL LIKE I'M SURROUNDED BY WALLS TODAY

06:24.843 --> 06:25.844
[sighs]

06:30.557 --> 06:32.642
[Chan] If it's okay with you,

06:33.393 --> 06:35.854
you can talk to me.

06:37.689 --> 06:38.982
I'll be away for a few weeks.

06:39.816 --> 06:43.528
I'm traveling around the East Coast
during vacation.

06:50.035 --> 06:51.036
[door closes]

06:52.495 --> 06:55.749
[Chan sighs] Hyeokchan,
you took my laptop.

06:55.832 --> 06:57.125
My research data is in there.

06:57.208 --> 06:59.419
[Hyeokchan]
I must've confused it with mine. Sorry.

06:59.502 --> 07:00.795
I'll send you the data.

07:00.879 --> 07:02.797
-Just use my laptop for now.
-[Chan sighs] I…

07:02.881 --> 07:04.174
[sighs]

07:04.257 --> 07:05.383
[laptop pings]

07:05.467 --> 07:08.094
-How do I turn off that sound?
-[Hyeokchan] The messenger alarm?

07:08.178 --> 07:10.055
Just mute it and ignore the messages

07:10.138 --> 07:13.016
or tell her I'm at the lab.

07:13.099 --> 07:14.893
Anyway, send me your email address.

07:14.976 --> 07:15.977
Hey.

07:16.061 --> 07:17.520
[echoing] Kang Hyeokchan!

07:17.604 --> 07:19.939
[fireworks exploding]

07:20.023 --> 07:22.233
[breathing heavily]

07:22.317 --> 07:25.904
[♪ Baroque music playing, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

07:30.075 --> 07:31.076
[Haran] Chan.

07:31.576 --> 07:32.577
I love you.

07:32.661 --> 07:34.079
I love you,

07:34.829 --> 07:36.539
Kang Hyeokchan. [chuckles]

07:36.623 --> 07:39.626
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-[breathing heavily]

07:59.604 --> 08:01.731
[footsteps echo]

08:05.860 --> 08:08.905
[Haran] Seonu Chan… who are you?

08:09.280 --> 08:12.367
[♪ melancholy music playing]

08:30.135 --> 08:31.136
Oh.

08:31.845 --> 08:34.180
Gosh, my eyes are so dry. [chuckles]

08:34.264 --> 08:35.598
Don't get the wrong idea.

08:35.682 --> 08:38.476
It's not like I have some big secret.
[chuckles, sniffles]

08:38.560 --> 08:39.978
Dry eyes?

08:40.061 --> 08:44.023
You follow me around, take photos of me,
then send them to my office.

08:44.107 --> 08:45.775
Why are you stalking me?

08:46.609 --> 08:48.903
-Stalking?
-I found an art museum ticket

08:48.987 --> 08:50.530
in your shirt,

08:50.613 --> 08:52.949
stamped with the date I went there.

08:53.033 --> 08:56.453
I did go to the art museum,
but I wasn't following you.

08:56.536 --> 08:58.371
-I just received a ticket.
-[sighs]

09:00.248 --> 09:02.542
You're the one who called my name, right?

09:04.794 --> 09:06.880
My name and my face.

09:06.963 --> 09:08.465
You couldn't have known.

09:09.841 --> 09:11.885
I guess you gathered a lot of info
while stalking me.

09:12.927 --> 09:13.970
I…

09:14.054 --> 09:17.515
I think this… will explain it.

09:17.599 --> 09:19.017
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

09:19.100 --> 09:24.522
I always check my partners' websites
before working with them. [chuckles]

09:24.606 --> 09:25.774
[sighs]

09:26.316 --> 09:29.360
You saw one photo and recognized me
from so far away? That's--

09:29.444 --> 09:32.447
I saw you up close earlier,
looking at the Sisley painting.

09:33.698 --> 09:36.534
Then why didn't you say so
when we met at our office?

09:36.618 --> 09:39.287
I'm sorry if I upset you
by not telling you about it.

09:42.123 --> 09:43.124
[sighs]

09:43.792 --> 09:46.836
I guess… I misunderstood.

09:47.879 --> 09:48.880
I'm sorry.

09:49.547 --> 09:50.757
[mumbles, clears throat]

10:02.435 --> 10:04.187
Then what are you doing at this hotel?

10:04.270 --> 10:05.522
I'm staying here.

10:05.605 --> 10:08.483
My company booked it for me
since it's close to Nana Atelier.

10:08.566 --> 10:11.694
Uh… Here's my card key. [chuckles]

10:12.278 --> 10:13.446
Room 3017.

10:15.532 --> 10:16.991
Then why did you run away--

10:17.075 --> 10:20.078
I wasn't running away.
I was just heading out…

10:20.787 --> 10:23.164
Because I forgot to buy this.

10:23.873 --> 10:26.084
It's my favorite. [chuckles softly]

10:26.167 --> 10:28.586
I didn't even know you were in the lobby.

10:29.170 --> 10:30.171
Yeah.

10:31.673 --> 10:34.008
Once again, I'm sorry.

10:34.717 --> 10:35.718
[mumbles]

10:44.227 --> 10:45.436
[sighs in relief]

10:49.691 --> 10:50.817
"Stalking"?

10:52.110 --> 10:54.028
[sighs] Darn it.

10:54.112 --> 10:56.364
Then who could have sent those photos?

10:57.991 --> 10:59.242
[Chan] Song Haran!

10:59.993 --> 11:00.994
[grunts]

11:02.162 --> 11:03.788
It's the stalker!

11:03.872 --> 11:06.040
[♪ tense music playing]

11:06.124 --> 11:07.792
Stalker!

11:09.460 --> 11:12.505
[Hayeong clicks tongue] You darn stalker!

11:13.006 --> 11:14.716
Don't you dare touch my sister!

11:14.799 --> 11:16.217
I'm reporting you!

11:18.344 --> 11:19.429
What is he doing here?

11:20.680 --> 11:22.599
[yelps, grunts]

11:24.767 --> 11:27.312
[gasps, sighs] Thank you.

11:29.522 --> 11:30.523
What?

11:33.276 --> 11:35.153
Stalker! Stalker!

11:35.945 --> 11:37.238
I'll get him.

11:37.322 --> 11:38.323
[Haran exclaims]

11:38.406 --> 11:40.909
[♪ tense music playing]

11:43.494 --> 11:44.662
[panting]

11:44.746 --> 11:45.997
[Haran breathes heavily]

11:53.671 --> 11:54.923
-[Haran squeals]
-[Chan grunts]

11:56.549 --> 11:58.718
-[Chan panting]
-[gasps]

11:59.427 --> 12:01.387
-Are you okay?
-[gasping]

12:01.471 --> 12:03.223
[footsteps thudding]

12:03.973 --> 12:05.975
[Chan and stalker grunting]

12:06.935 --> 12:09.312
[panting] Huh?

12:09.395 --> 12:11.189
[panting]

12:11.856 --> 12:15.193
[police siren wailing]

12:17.612 --> 12:18.988
[keyboard clacking]

12:19.072 --> 12:21.783
[officer bangs on table] Answer me.

12:21.866 --> 12:23.826
What was in that bottle?

12:25.536 --> 12:26.621
You'd better talk.

12:26.704 --> 12:28.539
Do you want to film a vlog in prison?

12:28.623 --> 12:30.500
Song Hayeong, be quiet.

12:31.793 --> 12:33.002
From the smell,

12:33.086 --> 12:36.005
it seemed like
a diluted sodium hypochlorite solution.

12:39.217 --> 12:41.094
Ah, I mean, NaClO.

12:41.678 --> 12:43.805
Sodium hypochlorite…

12:44.931 --> 12:48.184
I mean, it seemed similar to chlorine.

12:48.268 --> 12:49.769
[officer] Oh, chlorine?

12:49.852 --> 12:52.272
I guess you majored in that field.

12:53.523 --> 12:55.400
Why were you trying to throw that at her?

12:55.483 --> 12:57.026
I wanted to ruin her.

12:57.110 --> 12:59.404
She was always getting on my nerves.

13:01.072 --> 13:03.199
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

13:04.117 --> 13:05.493
Do you know each other?

13:06.160 --> 13:08.413
[Eunchan] The design contest winner is…

13:08.496 --> 13:10.331
-Song Haran!
-[cheering]

13:10.415 --> 13:11.541
Thank you!

13:11.624 --> 13:13.251
I'll treat everyone today.

13:13.334 --> 13:16.254
[stalker] I always wondered why
you were always at the center of attention

13:16.337 --> 13:18.172
and why everyone loved you.

13:18.756 --> 13:19.841
It was because of Kim Nana.

13:21.467 --> 13:24.887
You're lucky
your grandmother's a famous designer.

13:24.971 --> 13:27.598
I quit my job
because I hated the sight of you…

13:28.099 --> 13:31.060
[chuckles] but it's all because
of your grandma.

13:31.811 --> 13:33.313
You made me lose everything.

13:33.938 --> 13:36.774
Weren't you great
at pretending to be the main character

13:36.858 --> 13:39.944
and acting like you were happy
without a concern in the world?

13:40.403 --> 13:41.404
So why…

13:42.071 --> 13:43.531
Why now?

13:43.614 --> 13:46.034
-[Hayeong] Are you crazy?
-[officer] What are you doing?

13:47.243 --> 13:48.244
[sighs]

13:50.747 --> 13:52.248
I don't want to press charges.

13:52.915 --> 13:54.208
Just end this here, please.

13:55.793 --> 13:56.794
GEUMWON POLICE STATION

13:56.878 --> 13:58.963
[Hayeong groans] She ruined her own life.

13:59.047 --> 14:02.675
You went through so much
while you were at that company.

14:04.177 --> 14:06.763
But why were you here? And you, Mr. Yeon?

14:08.097 --> 14:10.516
[Hayeong] Oh... Well…

14:10.600 --> 14:14.854
The photos really bothered me,
so I had to do something.

14:14.979 --> 14:16.230
LOCATION TRACKER

14:16.314 --> 14:18.858
-What are you doing?
-There's a smudge on it.

14:18.941 --> 14:20.068
[breathing heavily]

14:20.151 --> 14:21.152
HARAN

14:21.235 --> 14:23.071
Something could really happen to Haran.

14:24.614 --> 14:27.200
I didn't dig through
your phone or anything.

14:27.283 --> 14:29.327
I just downloaded a location tracking app.

14:29.410 --> 14:31.746
But I saw you were here
when there was no meeting.

14:31.829 --> 14:34.415
-I got a bad feeling, so I came--
-Are you mad?

14:35.625 --> 14:36.667
Why would you do that?

14:37.335 --> 14:39.629
What if it really was someone dangerous?

14:39.712 --> 14:41.172
If something happened to you…

14:41.839 --> 14:44.759
[chuckles] Come on. I'm fine.

14:44.842 --> 14:46.594
Bad things don't come with a warning.

14:46.677 --> 14:48.763
People can get hurt in an instant.

14:48.846 --> 14:50.723
"What if I'd done something differently?"

14:50.807 --> 14:54.185
You can regret it hundreds,
thousands of times after the fact,

14:54.268 --> 14:55.520
but it won't change a thing.

14:55.603 --> 14:56.938
That's it!

14:57.021 --> 15:00.566
[sighs] Hayeong,
if anything happens to you too…

15:00.650 --> 15:02.985
Haran, look at me.

15:03.611 --> 15:04.779
Look at me.

15:05.363 --> 15:06.489
[breathes shakily]

15:07.532 --> 15:08.616
I'm right here.

15:09.367 --> 15:10.409
I'm okay.

15:11.327 --> 15:12.453
We're all fine.

15:12.537 --> 15:13.955
[panting]

15:14.038 --> 15:15.456
Nothing will happen now.

15:17.458 --> 15:18.459
It's okay.

15:20.962 --> 15:22.171
It's all right.

15:24.298 --> 15:26.717
You must have been startled. I'm sorry.

15:26.801 --> 15:29.512
But why were you running
with my sister earlier?

15:30.763 --> 15:32.056
Oh, well…

15:32.932 --> 15:35.977
My hotel was nearby. [chuckles]

15:36.060 --> 15:39.272
I spotted someone suspicious
following her, by coincidence.

15:39.355 --> 15:40.565
[in English] Wow.

15:40.648 --> 15:43.985
[in Korean] You're her savior.
Thank you so much for helping her...

15:45.319 --> 15:48.447
Thank you. [chuckles, inhales]

15:48.531 --> 15:50.366
Oh? [exclaims]

15:50.449 --> 15:51.659
Your jacket got bleached.

15:51.742 --> 15:53.077
Why did she have to throw…

15:53.161 --> 15:54.537
I'm sorry.

15:54.620 --> 15:56.330
I troubled you with a personal issue.

15:56.831 --> 15:58.916
And I'm sorry about earlier too.

15:59.000 --> 16:01.544
[stutters] It's fine.

16:01.627 --> 16:03.129
Then I'll head back now.

16:04.463 --> 16:06.424
-[Hayeong stutters] Bye, then.
-[Chan] Bye.

16:07.508 --> 16:09.552
What did you mean by
"sorry about earlier"?

16:09.635 --> 16:11.679
I grilled him, [sighs]

16:11.762 --> 16:13.431
thinking he was the stalker.

16:13.514 --> 16:16.184
Geez. Ungrateful much?

16:16.267 --> 16:18.728
He even ruined his jacket
trying to help you.

16:19.228 --> 16:20.396
[officer] Huh?

16:20.479 --> 16:22.940
Did the other guy leave?
He probably needs treatment.

16:23.024 --> 16:25.568
Hmm? Treatment? He just left.

16:26.569 --> 16:28.613
Hayeong, go home first.

16:28.696 --> 16:30.656
No, take me with you.

16:30.740 --> 16:32.241
I can't let you go alone.

16:32.325 --> 16:33.576
I'm really fine.

16:33.659 --> 16:35.411
And keep this a secret, okay?

16:36.287 --> 16:37.914
Don't report this to Grandma.

16:40.791 --> 16:42.001
Hurry home, okay?

16:42.084 --> 16:43.794
And keep your phone on.

16:45.588 --> 16:47.256
[sighs, groans]

16:47.924 --> 16:48.925
My heart…

16:50.301 --> 16:52.720
[sighs] I thought something might happen.

16:52.803 --> 16:54.055
Are you all right?

16:54.138 --> 16:55.139
Gosh.

16:55.681 --> 16:57.808
Of course. I'm fine.

16:57.892 --> 16:59.644
I'm always fine.

17:00.645 --> 17:03.272
Did you need something
approved by Grandma?

17:03.356 --> 17:04.899
Let's go. It's late.

17:05.858 --> 17:06.859
It's that way.

17:08.653 --> 17:10.029
Come on.

17:17.078 --> 17:18.079
Excuse me.

17:18.663 --> 17:19.872
Excuse me!

17:21.040 --> 17:22.124
No, not that way…

17:22.208 --> 17:23.542
Excuse me!

17:25.753 --> 17:26.921
Mr. Seonu.

17:28.256 --> 17:29.257
[Chan] Oh…

17:30.341 --> 17:32.552
[sighs] You hurt your hand earlier,
didn't you?

17:33.678 --> 17:36.138
I'm sorry I got you mixed up in this.

17:37.473 --> 17:39.767
Charge me for the hospital fees,
your jacket,

17:39.850 --> 17:42.144
and any inconveniences
caused by your injury--

17:42.228 --> 17:43.312
Are you a lawyer?

17:44.438 --> 17:46.399
I thought you were a designer.

17:46.482 --> 17:47.692
What?

17:48.526 --> 17:50.069
[♪ soft pleasant music playing]

17:50.152 --> 17:52.113
As you can see, I'm fine.

17:52.196 --> 17:53.990
So you don't have
to draw a line like that.

17:54.073 --> 17:56.033
I don't feel okay with it.

17:56.117 --> 17:57.868
I hate causing trouble for others.

18:06.961 --> 18:08.462
I'm really sorry about today.

18:08.546 --> 18:10.506
Make sure to get your hand treated.

18:21.392 --> 18:22.393
[Chan sighs]

18:24.145 --> 18:25.605
Why does this keep happening?

18:27.690 --> 18:28.941
It's scaring me.

18:33.070 --> 18:35.698
-[leaves rustling]
-[bird chirping]

18:35.781 --> 18:37.908
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

18:44.457 --> 18:46.917
[Yoon] She rejected me firmly.

18:47.001 --> 18:48.502
I want to live like this.

18:48.586 --> 18:49.879
I feel comfortable this way.

18:49.962 --> 18:52.965
I know I'm being stupid and weird.

18:54.425 --> 18:55.509
But…

18:56.927 --> 18:58.137
I'm too scared.

18:59.347 --> 19:01.057
-[door opens, closes]
-[sighs]

19:03.768 --> 19:04.935
[door closes]

19:09.774 --> 19:12.234
[exclaims] She's here.

19:12.318 --> 19:14.779
Don't do this anymore, Grandma.

19:15.363 --> 19:16.656
I'll handle things myself.

19:17.990 --> 19:19.450
Pushing everyone away

19:19.533 --> 19:22.036
and wasting time outside,
then hiding in a cave…

19:22.119 --> 19:23.871
Is that how you handle things?

19:23.954 --> 19:25.331
She…

19:25.414 --> 19:27.208
She was with a guy.

19:27.833 --> 19:29.585
-What?
-I was with them.

19:29.669 --> 19:33.297
I came home early,
and she spent more time with him alone.

19:33.381 --> 19:35.257
-Don't lie to me.
-I mean it.

19:35.341 --> 19:36.759
Mom, Dad. You saw it, right?

19:36.842 --> 19:37.968
I'm not lying, right?

19:38.552 --> 19:39.553
Is it true?

19:40.262 --> 19:41.806
I'll head upstairs first.

19:46.227 --> 19:48.938
Tell me. Who is he?
And what's their relationship?

19:50.064 --> 19:51.691
[♪ amusing music playing]

19:51.774 --> 19:52.858
Uh…

19:53.442 --> 19:54.860
Well…

19:54.944 --> 19:56.654
-They're just talking.
-"Talking"?

19:58.197 --> 20:01.742
Just leave her be.
Meddling will only ruin it.

20:02.827 --> 20:04.328
Then good night.

20:05.746 --> 20:06.747
Sleep tight.

20:10.084 --> 20:11.502
"Talking"?

20:13.838 --> 20:15.131
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

20:16.507 --> 20:18.509
Gosh, Song Hayeong.

20:18.592 --> 20:21.053
You've helped your sister again.

20:21.929 --> 20:23.472
This household is ruined without me.

20:23.556 --> 20:25.307
You're lucky to have such a great sister.

20:25.891 --> 20:27.393
You made her get the wrong idea.

20:27.476 --> 20:30.354
What? It's true that you were with a guy.

20:30.438 --> 20:32.648
Won't it be good for her
to get the wrong idea?

20:34.442 --> 20:36.193
Just pretend you're seeing someone.

20:36.277 --> 20:38.112
That will save you from a lot of nagging.

20:38.904 --> 20:41.323
No, there's no need to thank me.

20:41.907 --> 20:44.493
[inhales sharply] I'll take this instead.

20:45.870 --> 20:47.830
How is the animator's hand?

20:47.913 --> 20:49.999
I gave him my business card
so he can charge me.

20:50.082 --> 20:52.418
Business card? [sighs frustratingly]

20:52.501 --> 20:54.128
Did I raise you like that?

20:54.211 --> 20:57.298
If it weren't for him,
you would've gotten that chlorine…

20:57.381 --> 20:58.507
[in English] Oh God.

20:58.591 --> 21:00.384
[in Korean] Listen, Haran.

21:00.468 --> 21:03.679
You should at least buy him dinner
and thank him in person…

21:03.763 --> 21:05.598
[♪ whimsical music playing]

21:05.681 --> 21:08.309
But of course… [smacks lips]

21:09.018 --> 21:11.437
you're not the type to do that.

21:12.313 --> 21:15.149
Ah. Give him some new clothes.

21:15.232 --> 21:16.317
His jacket was ruined.

21:16.400 --> 21:18.194
Right. Clothes.

21:18.277 --> 21:19.904
Then next week at our meeting--

21:19.987 --> 21:21.155
Next week?

21:21.238 --> 21:24.784
He's here on a business trip.
He won't have many clothes.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.452
Would that be too late?

21:27.495 --> 21:29.121
-Then a delivery…
-Delivery?

21:29.205 --> 21:32.583
You should at least say,
"I'm sorry, your jacket's ruined."

21:32.666 --> 21:35.503
"I'm not sure if you'll like them,
but I got you some clothes."

21:35.586 --> 21:41.008
Shouldn't you at least give them to him
in person and show some sincerity?

21:42.301 --> 21:45.387
[sighs wearily] I'm tired.
I'm going to bed.

21:46.597 --> 21:47.973
[Haran] Hayeong.

21:48.599 --> 21:50.184
Thank you for today.

21:50.768 --> 21:54.814
[scoffs] You were telling me
to shut up earlier.

21:55.940 --> 21:56.941
Good night.

21:59.068 --> 22:00.694
[Haran] Bad things don't come
with a warning.

22:00.778 --> 22:02.696
People can get hurt in an instant.

22:02.780 --> 22:04.865
If something happened to you…

22:07.701 --> 22:08.702
What's this?

22:09.286 --> 22:11.247
Why are all our shoes in the bathtub?

22:11.872 --> 22:14.333
What do you mean? What shoes…

22:16.085 --> 22:18.337
I'm going to wash them.
They were pretty dirty.

22:18.420 --> 22:21.507
I have an exam in an hour.
What am I supposed to do?

22:21.590 --> 22:23.634
What is it? Are our shoes gone?

22:23.717 --> 22:25.094
How do I go to school today?

22:25.177 --> 22:27.388
I have an important meeting.

22:27.471 --> 22:29.473
You can all stay home today.

22:29.557 --> 22:31.767
-No, I have to go.
-Don't go!

22:32.351 --> 22:33.978
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

22:34.061 --> 22:36.063
Just don't go. [breathing heavily]

22:36.146 --> 22:38.566
What if something happens to you outside?

22:39.233 --> 22:40.776
It happened to Mom and Dad.

22:40.860 --> 22:43.904
So don't go, okay? Don't go!

22:44.488 --> 22:45.698
Haran…

22:45.781 --> 22:48.409
-Don't go.
-[Nana] It's okay. It's okay.

22:48.492 --> 22:49.618
Haran, it's all right.

22:49.702 --> 22:51.120
Just stay home.

22:51.203 --> 22:53.789
Don't go. Don't go. Please. Please.

22:53.873 --> 22:55.833
[♪ soft emotional music continuing]

22:58.669 --> 22:59.670
What?

23:00.546 --> 23:01.547
What?

23:01.630 --> 23:03.507
You just looked ugly. Good night.

23:04.758 --> 23:05.759
[door closes]

23:06.635 --> 23:08.137
[sighs, scoffs]

23:10.598 --> 23:11.599
[sighs heavily]

23:12.266 --> 23:13.434
Meet him in person?

23:14.393 --> 23:15.936
[doorbell rings]

23:16.020 --> 23:17.271
[Chan] Yes?

23:17.771 --> 23:18.856
[inhales sharply]

23:19.648 --> 23:20.691
What brings you here?

23:20.774 --> 23:23.819
Someone dropped this off for you
at the front desk.

23:23.903 --> 23:26.030
-Who?
-A young lady.

23:27.031 --> 23:29.325
She asked me to give this to you and left.

23:30.200 --> 23:32.202
[humming]

23:33.078 --> 23:34.079
[inhales sharply]

23:35.539 --> 23:36.832
How did she know my room number?

23:38.292 --> 23:40.920
Ah. My card key.

23:41.503 --> 23:43.589
[Haran] I'm sorry your jacket's ruined.

23:43.672 --> 23:46.425
I'm not sure if you'll like them,
but I got you some clothes.

23:46.508 --> 23:49.011
-[thunderclap]
-[rain pattering]

23:49.720 --> 23:50.721
Huh?

23:53.974 --> 23:55.184
[exclaims] No.

23:55.267 --> 23:56.602
No.

23:56.685 --> 23:57.728
Don't get involved.

24:00.105 --> 24:02.942
Please, please, please don't be here.

24:10.366 --> 24:12.368
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

24:13.702 --> 24:15.579
[rain pattering]

24:17.414 --> 24:19.708
[Haran] You know that particular smell
before it rains?

24:21.043 --> 24:22.795
I love that smell.

24:23.587 --> 24:26.924
But it disappears so quickly,
so I just stand there smelling it.

24:28.092 --> 24:31.553
But the catch is that
you always end up with a nasty cold.

24:58.831 --> 25:00.040
[Chan] From the smell,

25:00.124 --> 25:02.835
it seemed like
a diluted sodium hypochlorite solution.

25:02.918 --> 25:04.628
Ah, I mean, NaClO.

25:04.712 --> 25:07.881
[Haran] There's another guy
who speaks like him.

25:08.257 --> 25:09.425
[inaudible]

25:13.345 --> 25:14.388
Ah…

25:14.471 --> 25:16.098
You'll catch a cold.

25:16.181 --> 25:18.559
You came here because of me, so take this.

25:19.435 --> 25:23.313
[♪ Baroque music on earphones, J.S. Bach
"Goldberg Variations, BWV 988: Aria"]

25:27.109 --> 25:28.902
No, it's okay.

25:28.986 --> 25:30.571
I'm the one who's not okay.

25:34.783 --> 25:36.368
[thunder rumbles]

25:36.452 --> 25:37.953
Oh… [grunts]

25:38.037 --> 25:40.664
I have another one in my room.
I'll go get it.

25:41.331 --> 25:42.875
-Hang on.
-No, I…

25:44.293 --> 25:45.794
[woman] Hey! Haran!

25:46.378 --> 25:47.379
[woman gasps]

25:48.047 --> 25:50.215
Song Haran! You're actually alive!

25:50.299 --> 25:51.717
[exclaims] Gosh.

25:51.800 --> 25:57.139
You suddenly cut all contact with us
and said you were going to the US.

25:57.222 --> 26:00.559
I went to your workplace, but you quit,
and your number wasn't in service.

26:00.642 --> 26:02.352
I was so worried about you.

26:02.895 --> 26:04.146
I'm glad I bumped into you.

26:04.229 --> 26:06.190
I actually booked a wedding here.

26:06.273 --> 26:07.441
It's next spring.

26:07.524 --> 26:09.902
-You'll be able to see everyone--
-Sorry, Yujeong.

26:09.985 --> 26:12.196
I'm in a hurry right now. Sorry.

26:12.279 --> 26:13.280
Huh?

26:13.781 --> 26:14.990
Haran, wait!

26:15.616 --> 26:16.700
Haran!

26:19.870 --> 26:22.247
-I'll come with you to get the umbrella.
-Pardon?

26:22.831 --> 26:24.333
Huh? Why isn't it here?

26:24.416 --> 26:25.667
[stutters] Hang on.

26:26.210 --> 26:28.462
Ben, my umbrella… Mmm…

26:28.545 --> 26:29.713
Is he not here?

26:29.797 --> 26:31.048
Oh, the concierge…

26:31.131 --> 26:32.841
No, it's fine.

26:33.675 --> 26:34.676
Hello?

26:34.760 --> 26:37.679
Hello. It's Room 3017.

26:37.763 --> 26:40.599
[clock ticking]

26:40.682 --> 26:43.018
[♪ whimsical music playing]

26:55.989 --> 26:57.616
It's taking a while.

26:59.743 --> 27:00.869
I'm sure they'll come.

27:01.662 --> 27:02.663
Right.

27:12.881 --> 27:14.883
-[door beeps, opens]
-Oh! The umbrella…

27:14.967 --> 27:17.344
No, it's Ben.

27:18.095 --> 27:19.930
-Ben.
-[Ben] Oh.

27:20.013 --> 27:21.098
Where were you?

27:21.181 --> 27:24.393
My mother-in-law wanted
to give me some chicken stew.

27:24.476 --> 27:26.520
Oh? Ms. Song?

27:26.603 --> 27:27.646
Hello.

27:27.729 --> 27:30.148
I was dropping off something
and came to borrow an umbrella.

27:30.232 --> 27:32.192
Oh! This is great.

27:32.276 --> 27:33.902
-You can have a meal with us…
-[shouts]

27:34.653 --> 27:35.988
[Chan] An umbrella! [grunts]

27:36.071 --> 27:38.031
-Here. [chuckles]
-[♪ amusing music playing]

27:38.115 --> 27:39.575
You can take this.

27:40.409 --> 27:43.495
-It's pouring, so get home safely.
-Right.

27:43.579 --> 27:46.915
I'll see you at our next meeting.

27:48.876 --> 27:50.043
Bye.

27:50.961 --> 27:52.671
[Chan sighing]

27:56.049 --> 27:59.720
What was that?
You become an idiot in front of Ms. Song.

27:59.803 --> 28:01.054
Is there something going on?

28:01.138 --> 28:02.431
Are you dating?

28:02.514 --> 28:03.932
[sighs wearily]

28:04.766 --> 28:06.310
There is something…

28:07.227 --> 28:08.854
But there shouldn't be.

28:09.855 --> 28:11.023
Ben.

28:11.523 --> 28:13.567
Don't you feel suffocated in this hotel?

28:14.151 --> 28:16.528
Should we just rent a house
while we're here?

28:16.612 --> 28:20.115
Is it the hotel or your own heart
that's suffocating you?

28:20.198 --> 28:22.284
-[Ben laughs]
-[sighs wearily, groans]

28:22.367 --> 28:24.870
[Manjae grunting]

28:27.331 --> 28:28.540
[grunts]

28:28.624 --> 28:30.959
[groans, exhales heavily]

28:31.043 --> 28:32.085
[grunts]

28:32.169 --> 28:34.046
-[groaning]
-[♪ grim music playing]

28:34.129 --> 28:35.380
[barks]

28:35.464 --> 28:37.633
-[whining softly]
-[Manjae groaning]

28:39.134 --> 28:40.427
[groaning]

28:40.510 --> 28:41.762
[barking]

28:43.221 --> 28:45.766
SHIM
Coffee House

28:49.019 --> 28:50.562
It must be closed today.

28:50.646 --> 28:52.773
We've been waiting,
but Mr. Park's not coming.

28:52.856 --> 28:53.857
Thank you.

28:53.941 --> 28:55.359
[woman] Where should we go?

28:57.694 --> 28:58.904
Hey, Genius.

28:59.404 --> 29:00.405
[door thuds shut]

29:03.492 --> 29:05.160
[gasps, mumbles]

29:10.415 --> 29:12.417
I'LL BE BACK SOON

29:16.755 --> 29:17.965
-[man whispers] Hello?
-[gasps softly]

29:19.049 --> 29:20.884
Isn't this Mr. Park's phone?

29:20.968 --> 29:23.261
It is, but he's asleep right now.

29:23.345 --> 29:25.097
[Manjae] I'll take that.

29:25.722 --> 29:27.516
-Hello?
-Hello?

29:29.267 --> 29:31.895
-[camera clicking]
-[Hadam coos, gasps]

29:31.979 --> 29:35.732
-Give me your paw. Good boy! [squeals]
-[camera clicks]

29:35.816 --> 29:38.652
-[giggles] Hi, I'm Genius.
-[♪ happy music playing]

29:38.735 --> 29:40.779
Aren't I big and adorable?

29:40.862 --> 29:42.197
Why is there a dog here?

29:42.280 --> 29:45.909
The owner of a coffee shop
Big Sis is a regular at was hospitalized,

29:45.993 --> 29:47.744
so she said she'd take care of him.

29:47.828 --> 29:49.871
[groans] I wish I could keep him.

29:49.955 --> 29:52.165
Song Hayeong, that little brat.

29:52.249 --> 29:54.042
What? It wasn't Hayeong.

29:54.126 --> 29:55.377
[♪ amusing music playing]

29:55.460 --> 29:57.087
-What?
-You're here.

29:57.587 --> 30:00.674
[Hadam sighs] Park Genius.
Isn't that such a cute name?

30:00.757 --> 30:02.718
He was named after the coffee shop owner.

30:02.801 --> 30:04.970
-His name's--
-Hadam. Your academy.

30:05.053 --> 30:07.764
[gasps, groans]

30:07.848 --> 30:11.309
Hey, Genius. I'll be back soon. See you.

30:11.393 --> 30:12.894
See you, Grandma.

30:15.981 --> 30:19.067
Were you close enough to someone
to look after their dog?

30:19.151 --> 30:21.153
[chuckles nervously]
Sorry, I brought him without asking.

30:21.236 --> 30:23.363
-[Genius slurping]
-[coos]

30:24.156 --> 30:25.282
[Haran chuckles]

30:27.325 --> 30:29.077
[♪ pleasant music playing]

30:31.496 --> 30:33.623
WE MISS YOU

30:33.707 --> 30:35.917
GET PLENTY OF REST AND FOCUS ON RECOVERING

30:42.549 --> 30:44.843
Should I get some toys for Genius?

30:47.012 --> 30:49.556
You're a dog, and this is a yard.

30:50.891 --> 30:52.768
Run around all you want.

30:53.351 --> 30:54.936
[whines]

30:55.729 --> 30:57.647
-[doorbell rings]
-[Nana sighs]

30:59.149 --> 31:01.276
-[Nana] Who is it?
-[man] Excuse me.

31:03.153 --> 31:04.738
Hello.

31:04.821 --> 31:07.365
-Is my dog Genius here?
-[Genius barks]

31:07.449 --> 31:08.450
Hey, Genius!

31:09.409 --> 31:11.495
-Genius!
-[Genius barks]

31:11.578 --> 31:14.623
[exclaims] Good boy.

31:14.706 --> 31:17.626
You must have been startled
being here without me.

31:17.709 --> 31:19.878
-Good boy.
-Hello.

31:19.961 --> 31:20.962
[Manjae] Ah…

31:21.046 --> 31:23.840
My eldest granddaughter
isn't here right now.

31:23.924 --> 31:26.259
Gosh. Where are my manners?

31:26.343 --> 31:29.012
Thank you so much
for taking care of Genius.

31:29.638 --> 31:32.224
It's fine. It wasn't hard
taking care of him.

31:32.808 --> 31:34.142
But how did you…

31:34.226 --> 31:35.644
I got discharged early.

31:36.228 --> 31:38.772
I heard it was the house
with the coffee-colored door.

31:38.855 --> 31:42.651
I was worried I'd come to the wrong house
for a moment. [chuckles]

31:42.734 --> 31:45.070
I'll thank you formally next time.

31:45.987 --> 31:47.614
-Let's go, Genius.
-Goodbye.

31:47.697 --> 31:48.698
[Manjae] Bye.

31:49.199 --> 31:50.867
[♪ dreamy music playing]

31:50.951 --> 31:54.037
[Hadam] Park Genius.
Isn't that such a cute name?

31:54.121 --> 31:55.997
He was named after the coffee shop owner.

31:56.081 --> 31:58.458
-His name's--
-Park Manjae?

31:59.334 --> 32:01.920
Are you Manjae, who lived in Chuncheon?

32:07.384 --> 32:08.385
Who…

32:08.468 --> 32:09.636
It really is you.

32:09.719 --> 32:11.805
It's me.
The house with the persimmon tree.

32:12.973 --> 32:13.974
Who?

32:17.727 --> 32:19.396
PARK MANJAE

32:19.479 --> 32:22.107
[♪ playing romantic music,
"La Vie En Rose"]

32:32.993 --> 32:35.120
Manjae!

32:36.079 --> 32:37.706
Manjae!

32:37.789 --> 32:39.457
Nabong!

32:39.541 --> 32:42.043
[♪ romantic music playing]

32:44.504 --> 32:46.381
[inaudible]

32:54.764 --> 32:57.893
The fashionista Nabong from Chuncheon?

32:57.976 --> 32:59.436
[giggles]

32:59.519 --> 33:00.729
Yes, it's me.

33:00.812 --> 33:02.439
It's Nabong.

33:02.522 --> 33:03.773
It really is you?

33:03.857 --> 33:04.858
[both laughing]

33:04.941 --> 33:08.028
You're really Nabong? [laughs]

33:12.282 --> 33:13.283
Huh?

33:23.960 --> 33:25.670
Huh? That's…

33:27.088 --> 33:31.009
[Chan] Mr. Park, the clutter box
you're throwing away… [exclaims]

33:34.930 --> 33:36.848
[grunts] Hello.

33:36.932 --> 33:39.309
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]
-What are you doing here?

33:40.894 --> 33:42.979
I'm going to live here. What about you?

33:43.063 --> 33:45.941
You're living here? Why?

33:46.775 --> 33:48.568
I'm close with Mr. Park.

33:48.652 --> 33:51.238
-What brings you here?
-Why are you close?

33:52.155 --> 33:53.365
Why?

33:54.074 --> 33:57.661
The hotel's nearby,
so I came here every day.

33:58.411 --> 34:01.581
And I actually received the exhibit ticket
from Mr. Park

34:01.665 --> 34:02.958
after fixing the ice machine.

34:03.041 --> 34:05.543
Then the regular
who fixed the ice machine…

34:08.463 --> 34:10.757
But why stay here instead of a nice hotel?

34:15.929 --> 34:17.847
-[Chan grunts]
-[Manjae exhales heavily]

34:17.931 --> 34:19.557
You heard the doctor, right?

34:19.641 --> 34:22.060
Make sure to take your meds
and get plenty of sleep.

34:22.143 --> 34:24.312
And no overworking or drinking alcohol.

34:24.396 --> 34:25.772
Enough with the nagging.

34:26.564 --> 34:28.149
My ears are going to bleed.

34:28.525 --> 34:30.902
-Gosh.
-Goodness.

34:30.986 --> 34:34.239
There's nothing like being back home.
[sighs contentedly]

34:34.322 --> 34:38.368
[inhales sharply]
There are a lot of rooms here.

34:38.451 --> 34:41.454
Oh. It's a bit big for one person.

34:41.538 --> 34:44.624
-Mmm-hmm. You must feel lonely--
-[Manjae sighs heavily]

34:44.708 --> 34:47.002
Mr. Park, can you let me
stay in one of the rooms?

34:47.585 --> 34:50.213
Just for three months.
[chuckles] Three months.

34:50.297 --> 34:54.301
I was going to rent a house,
but he had some empty rooms.

34:55.427 --> 34:58.388
And Ben is at his in-law's.
[chuckles softly]

34:58.471 --> 34:59.806
So what brings you here?

34:59.889 --> 35:02.392
Then the regular
who called an ambulance for him…

35:02.976 --> 35:05.437
Hang on. Then it was you
who answered the phone?

35:05.520 --> 35:10.483
Ah. I heard the regular I talked to
on the phone was taking care of Genius.

35:10.567 --> 35:13.153
Yes, that regular is me.

35:13.236 --> 35:15.530
Ah. Regular.

35:16.698 --> 35:17.866
Regular… Mmm.

35:20.827 --> 35:25.081
I think Mr. Park
was around here somewhere.

35:25.165 --> 35:26.958
By the way, is he all right?

35:27.042 --> 35:28.835
[Manjae] I'm all right.

35:30.545 --> 35:33.131
They said
it's variant angina or something.

35:34.716 --> 35:36.259
I just have to take medicine.

35:37.093 --> 35:39.304
By the way, it's been so long.

35:39.387 --> 35:42.891
You suddenly disappeared
from Chuncheon one day.

35:42.974 --> 35:45.101
It's been over 50 years.

35:45.185 --> 35:48.855
But I'm quite famous now.
You really didn't know?

35:48.938 --> 35:51.524
Well, I knew the name Nana Kim,

35:51.608 --> 35:54.694
but I never imagined
it would be you. [laughs]

35:54.778 --> 35:58.907
Gosh, you were always
going on about la vie en rose,

35:58.990 --> 36:02.827
and you really went to France
and achieved that dream.

36:02.911 --> 36:04.579
[both chuckling]

36:04.663 --> 36:09.668
But I've been running a coffee shop
in this neighborhood for over 10 years.

36:09.751 --> 36:13.672
How is it that
we never ran into each other?

36:13.755 --> 36:15.382
That's how the world is.

36:16.049 --> 36:19.803
It can feel small at times
but big at others. [chuckles softly]

36:19.886 --> 36:23.932
But how did you get so close
to my granddaughter?

36:24.015 --> 36:26.976
She never lets anyone get close to her.

36:27.060 --> 36:29.979
She's a regular at my coffee shop.

36:30.063 --> 36:33.525
She stays there
almost every day until I close.

36:35.485 --> 36:37.987
I wondered where she was staying out
so late every day.

36:38.738 --> 36:40.073
She was there?

36:40.156 --> 36:41.449
[♪ soft sentimental music playing]

36:41.533 --> 36:42.867
[chuckles softly]

36:42.951 --> 36:44.369
I guess she felt more at ease

36:45.620 --> 36:48.289
at your coffee shop than at home with me.

36:49.124 --> 36:51.501
I guess you did something for her
that I couldn't.

36:52.168 --> 36:55.255
-Thanks.
-All I did was give her coffee.

36:55.338 --> 36:56.881
I didn't do anything special.

36:59.300 --> 37:00.510
It's been seven years,

37:01.511 --> 37:03.805
but I never knew

37:05.306 --> 37:07.058
she had a place to rely on.

37:07.142 --> 37:08.143
Seven years?

37:09.227 --> 37:12.939
That's around the time I first met her.

37:14.232 --> 37:15.775
I think it was around summer.

37:16.818 --> 37:19.028
I'm not sure if it's okay to ask this,

37:19.779 --> 37:22.240
but did something happen to her

37:22.907 --> 37:24.242
back then?

37:28.455 --> 37:29.956
[rain pattering]

37:32.250 --> 37:34.753
-[shop bell chimes]
-[Manjae exclaiming]

37:35.795 --> 37:36.838
My gosh.

37:37.839 --> 37:40.592
Hey, Genius.

37:41.092 --> 37:42.719
It's raining cats and dogs.

37:43.261 --> 37:44.888
It's pouring, isn't it?

37:45.972 --> 37:51.186
It was a day when it suddenly poured.

37:52.312 --> 37:54.314
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

37:56.816 --> 37:59.319
But she was sitting in the rain,

38:00.195 --> 38:01.362
crying.

38:01.446 --> 38:03.448
[sobbing]

38:06.326 --> 38:08.661
[Nana] Her boyfriend died back then.

38:09.579 --> 38:12.707
He went to study in Boston,
but he suddenly died.

38:12.791 --> 38:14.667
[♪ soft emotional music continues]

38:24.469 --> 38:26.095
[cell phone ringing]

38:27.055 --> 38:28.056
[box thuds]

38:30.934 --> 38:32.227
-[grunts]
-[ringing continues]

38:32.310 --> 38:33.812
[chuckles nervously, grunts]

38:35.480 --> 38:36.606
[Chan exclaims]

38:37.816 --> 38:38.900
[groans, inhales sharply]

38:38.983 --> 38:40.527
BEN

38:41.236 --> 38:42.237
[groans]

38:43.238 --> 38:45.573
[stammers] You're getting a call…

38:45.657 --> 38:46.699
Can you…

38:47.283 --> 38:50.370
Can you hold it
on the other side? [grunts softly]

38:51.621 --> 38:53.122
[grunts, inhales sharply]

38:53.957 --> 38:55.250
Yes.

38:55.333 --> 38:56.626
Hey, Ben.

38:57.335 --> 38:59.045
[stutters] A meeting on Monday?

38:59.128 --> 39:01.005
Okay. Bye.

39:02.131 --> 39:04.551
Thank you. Can you put it here?

39:05.260 --> 39:06.845
-Right. [grunts]
-[door opens]

39:06.928 --> 39:08.054
[exclaims]

39:08.137 --> 39:10.348
[in English] I'm back!

39:10.431 --> 39:12.058
Genius, house!

39:12.141 --> 39:13.768
[in Korean] Were you at our house?

39:14.352 --> 39:17.313
You only just got discharged.
You should've called me.

39:17.397 --> 39:21.234
It's the first time I've heard you talk
this much in seven years.

39:21.317 --> 39:23.653
[chuckles awkwardly] Are you all right?

39:23.736 --> 39:25.405
Yes, thanks to you.

39:25.488 --> 39:30.159
But it's a surprise seeing
my VVIP regulars here together.

39:30.243 --> 39:31.327
[chuckles]

39:31.411 --> 39:33.288
Roomie, say hi. She's…

39:33.371 --> 39:35.456
Oh. I know her.

39:35.540 --> 39:38.126
She's a designer
at the company I'm working with.

39:38.209 --> 39:40.795
You were working with Nabong…

39:40.879 --> 39:43.506
I mean, the designer Nana Kim?

39:43.590 --> 39:45.800
How do you know my grandmother's name?

39:45.884 --> 39:47.886
It turns out she was my childhood friend.

39:47.969 --> 39:49.262
Oh, really?

39:49.345 --> 39:52.098
We lived in the same neighborhood
for 10 years, but I never knew.

39:52.181 --> 39:53.474
I was so excited,

39:53.558 --> 39:56.436
-I almost did a backflip.
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]

39:56.519 --> 39:57.896
[laughs]

39:58.938 --> 40:00.690
Right, I forgot.

40:00.773 --> 40:02.066
Thank you.

40:02.150 --> 40:05.278
You locked the doors for me
and even looked after Genius.

40:05.361 --> 40:06.446
It's nothing.

40:06.529 --> 40:09.616
And you can talk to me informally.
You're Grandma's friend.

40:09.699 --> 40:12.952
Then should I start
talking to you casually?

40:13.745 --> 40:14.787
Like a friend.

40:14.871 --> 40:16.956
-Ah. Yes.
-[Manjae chuckles]

40:17.457 --> 40:19.751
This is the first time
I've seen you smile like that too.

40:19.834 --> 40:21.002
[chuckles awkwardly]

40:21.628 --> 40:24.422
But… you must feel comfortable
on your own.

40:24.505 --> 40:26.466
Why did you let him live here?

40:26.549 --> 40:28.009
[clears throat]

40:28.676 --> 40:31.554
I thought I'd feel safer
if there was someone with me.

40:32.347 --> 40:34.849
And he's adorable.

40:35.850 --> 40:38.061
He's a really good man.

40:39.562 --> 40:41.356
Come sit down. I'll make you coffee.

40:41.439 --> 40:43.358
No, it's fine. Get some rest.

40:43.441 --> 40:46.361
Even if I don't drink coffee,

40:46.444 --> 40:49.656
is it okay to stay here
until closing hours?

40:51.074 --> 40:55.536
You're young.
You should be having fun outside.

40:56.037 --> 40:58.289
You shouldn't stay cooped up
in this boring place.

40:58.373 --> 41:00.375
This place is the most fun for me.

41:00.458 --> 41:01.668
I can focus on work,

41:01.751 --> 41:04.754
and I feel at ease
because it feels like nothing will happen.

41:05.588 --> 41:06.589
Mmm.

41:11.302 --> 41:12.512
[elevator dings]

41:16.516 --> 41:19.519
Bring the dancheong data
I mentioned to my office.

41:19.602 --> 41:21.354
I'll give you the files now.

41:21.437 --> 41:23.773
[cell phone vibrating]

41:23.856 --> 41:25.483
If it's a work call, take it.

41:25.566 --> 41:26.734
Mr. Yeon, take the files.

41:26.818 --> 41:27.902
-Sure.
-Here.

41:30.363 --> 41:32.115
-Hello.
-Here, Ms. Kim.

41:32.198 --> 41:34.450
I called about the fabric materials.

41:34.534 --> 41:37.036
Yes, I'd like the 0.8 mm ones.

41:37.120 --> 41:39.372
SEONU CHAN

41:39.455 --> 41:41.499
-Ah, yes.
-[Nana] She…

41:41.582 --> 41:43.376
-Thank you.
-[Nana] She was with a guy.

41:44.335 --> 41:46.879
[♪ amusing music playing]

42:09.610 --> 42:12.488
[Ben] It's an original character
that Chan created.

42:12.572 --> 42:16.075
That character. Was it based on someone?

42:17.410 --> 42:19.287
No, it just came to mind.

42:20.455 --> 42:24.667
He drew his ideal type,
but he met her in real life?

42:27.754 --> 42:31.090
Mr. Yeon, keep an eye on Ms. Song

42:32.050 --> 42:33.217
and Seonu Chan.

42:33.968 --> 42:35.136
Yes, ma'am.

42:41.017 --> 42:42.977
[exclaims] That expression.

42:43.061 --> 42:46.230
You look like a robot that's been given
an order you can't refuse.

42:46.314 --> 42:48.441
-It's not like that.
-[♪ playful music playing]

42:48.524 --> 42:49.984
What is it? Did Grandma…

42:50.943 --> 42:53.446
I mean, did Ms. Kim order you
to do something again?

42:53.529 --> 42:54.572
No, she didn't.

42:54.655 --> 42:56.491
"No, she didn't"?

42:56.574 --> 42:58.785
All right. Then keep working
in your robot mode.

42:58.868 --> 43:00.995
Beep, beep, beep.

43:01.662 --> 43:03.664
[Hayeong imitating robot beeping]

43:04.957 --> 43:08.002
[chuckles] It's pretty fun teasing him.

43:08.086 --> 43:09.420
[Chan] Let's take a photo.

43:09.504 --> 43:10.546
One plus one is what?

43:10.630 --> 43:11.756
[all] Two.

43:11.839 --> 43:12.965
[camera clicks]

43:14.217 --> 43:15.343
[Hayeong exclaims]

43:16.844 --> 43:18.679
[Seung-gyu] I'm a huge animation fan.

43:18.763 --> 43:20.014
Where did you learn art?

43:20.098 --> 43:21.307
At CalArts.

43:21.390 --> 43:25.353
[exclaims] CalArts? That's insane!

43:25.436 --> 43:29.065
-Sweetie, can you draw me a caricature…
-[Hayeong and Sol laugh]

43:29.148 --> 43:31.317
-…with your professional skills?
-Sure.

43:31.400 --> 43:32.527
[Hayeong] Me too.

43:32.610 --> 43:33.611
-[Seung-gyu] Me too.
-What?

43:33.694 --> 43:35.905
-[Sol] I'll get some paper.
-When did they get so close?

43:35.988 --> 43:37.490
Is he a capybara or what?

43:38.157 --> 43:39.617
[Remy] Is this better, or this?

43:40.326 --> 43:42.495
-[Seung-gyu] The second one.
-[Remy] Is this better?

43:43.871 --> 43:45.414
How should I pose for this?

43:45.498 --> 43:46.624
Like this?

43:46.833 --> 43:48.251
[Chan] Hmm. [sighs]

43:49.585 --> 43:51.254
Using a dancheong pattern

43:51.337 --> 43:54.549
to show that she's Korean
just with her outfit…

43:55.341 --> 43:58.344
Wow. This might be a problem.

44:01.264 --> 44:03.099
Because it's so good. [chuckles]

44:05.726 --> 44:10.523
Then let's develop this
with dancheong as the basic concept.

44:10.606 --> 44:13.901
All right. I'll send this to HQ
and schedule a video call.

44:15.820 --> 44:18.698
-I feel a bit hungry.
-[♪ whimsical music playing]

44:18.781 --> 44:22.201
I'd like to continue our discussion
over dinner. Are you free?

44:22.285 --> 44:24.412
Yes, I'd love that.

44:24.495 --> 44:26.539
How about the new
Italian restaurant nearby?

44:26.622 --> 44:27.832
It seemed really wild.

44:29.125 --> 44:32.837
Your appetite must be wild too.
No wonder your jawline disappeared.

44:36.465 --> 44:37.466
Have dinner without me.

44:41.971 --> 44:42.972
What do you like?

44:43.598 --> 44:45.183
You can eat without me. I--

44:45.266 --> 44:47.768
You're joining.
I said we're discussing work.

44:52.857 --> 44:55.067
[♪ elegant piano music
playing on speakers]

45:04.160 --> 45:06.412
They look good together.

45:07.121 --> 45:08.206
What?

45:09.624 --> 45:11.959
I said the interior is nice.

45:16.881 --> 45:18.341
Hello?

45:18.424 --> 45:19.926
All right.

45:20.927 --> 45:23.888
Sorry, I have to go.
Something urgent came up.

45:23.971 --> 45:25.014
Then let's--

45:25.097 --> 45:27.308
Sit. I didn't mean you were going.

45:28.726 --> 45:31.103
I'm sorry. Enjoy your dinner.

45:31.979 --> 45:33.022
See you at the meeting,

45:33.105 --> 45:36.484
Animator Seonu Chan.

45:37.735 --> 45:39.362
Right. I'll see you at the meeting.

45:47.787 --> 45:51.207
[inhales sharply]
If you feel uncomfortable, we can just…

45:51.290 --> 45:52.833
Here are the menus.

45:53.834 --> 45:55.962
I'm sorry, but we'll just…

45:57.797 --> 46:02.760
[Hayeong] You should at least buy him
dinner and thank him in person…

46:02.843 --> 46:04.136
Let's just eat.

46:04.220 --> 46:05.846
I'll buy.

46:05.930 --> 46:07.056
What?

46:07.139 --> 46:09.767
Ah. Okay…

46:12.436 --> 46:14.021
Can you recommend something?

46:14.105 --> 46:17.108
-Take your time. Just look here.
-Ah.

46:17.191 --> 46:20.653
Our rollatini is our signature dish,
made with sliced eggplants…

46:20.736 --> 46:23.864
-She doesn't like eggplants.
-How did you know I don't like eggplants?

46:25.074 --> 46:26.575
What? Oh…

46:27.868 --> 46:29.537
Many people dislike eggplants.

46:29.620 --> 46:31.289
Right?

46:31.372 --> 46:32.748
-[waiter] Right…
-Me too.

46:32.832 --> 46:34.834
I dislike them as well.

46:34.917 --> 46:37.795
Can you just give me
something you can prepare quickly?

46:37.878 --> 46:40.006
-Me too.
-All right.

46:43.342 --> 46:44.510
[sighs contentedly]

46:44.593 --> 46:47.680
-The interior really is nice.
-[cell phone buzzes]

46:48.431 --> 46:49.432
[Chan sighs]

46:50.016 --> 46:52.810
[Nana] Repetition means
your heart has already stirred.

46:52.893 --> 46:56.147
Instead of writing his name over and over,
follow your heart.

46:56.230 --> 46:57.273
"Name"?

46:58.524 --> 46:59.942
[Nana] Mr. Yeon, take the files.

47:08.909 --> 47:10.202
[sighs, mumbles]

47:11.037 --> 47:12.705
Let me apologize first.

47:14.707 --> 47:15.750
SEONU CHAN

47:15.833 --> 47:17.960
Oh? Why is my name there?

47:18.044 --> 47:19.170
Well…

47:20.212 --> 47:23.424
I wrote this when I thought
you were my stalker,

47:23.507 --> 47:26.927
but I think Ms. Kim saw this
and thought I had feelings for you.

47:27.011 --> 47:29.638
That's probably why
we ended up having dinner alone.

47:29.722 --> 47:31.057
Ah…

47:31.849 --> 47:32.933
[sighs]

47:34.143 --> 47:35.519
I'll explain this to her…

47:35.603 --> 47:38.147
[Hayeong] Just pretend
you're seeing someone.

47:38.230 --> 47:41.192
That will save you from a lot of nagging.

47:41.275 --> 47:44.236
I should tell her…

47:45.237 --> 47:46.781
But is it okay if I don't?

47:47.865 --> 47:49.158
Pardon?

47:49.241 --> 47:50.743
It's a bit complicated,

47:50.826 --> 47:53.412
but I think
this will be a good opportunity

47:53.496 --> 47:55.581
to put my grandmother's mind at ease.

47:56.332 --> 47:59.251
Oh. Sure.

48:00.044 --> 48:02.463
If it helps you, then it's fine with me.

48:03.422 --> 48:06.300
Thank you. I'll make sure
this won't cause you any trouble.

48:07.009 --> 48:08.094
All right.

48:08.177 --> 48:09.470
[speaker squeaks]

48:09.553 --> 48:10.554
[grunts]

48:10.638 --> 48:12.932
[high-pitched ringing]

48:16.060 --> 48:19.230
There must have been
an issue with the connection. I'm sorry.

48:19.313 --> 48:20.648
It's fine.

48:20.731 --> 48:23.150
[♪ elegant classical music
playing on speakers]

48:31.617 --> 48:33.160
[Nana] How did the two seem?

48:34.370 --> 48:36.205
[Taeseok] I'm not sure yet.

48:36.288 --> 48:37.289
REPRESENTATIVE
KIM NANA

48:38.290 --> 48:40.584
I set things up for them,
so we'll know soon.

48:41.627 --> 48:43.879
-You can go now.
-I'll take you home.

48:43.963 --> 48:45.840
I'm not a child. I can go home by myself.

48:46.507 --> 48:49.176
You don't look well these days.

48:49.260 --> 48:51.720
And you haven't gotten
any checkups for years.

48:53.889 --> 48:56.600
At least take these. They're vitamins.

48:58.394 --> 49:01.272
You're not my chauffeur
or secretary anymore.

49:01.772 --> 49:05.025
If you've become the COO,
you should stop doing such things.

49:05.109 --> 49:07.778
Why would a COO take care
of my granddaughters as well?

49:08.571 --> 49:10.489
I'm doing it because I want to.

49:11.073 --> 49:12.324
Then don't work too late.

49:19.165 --> 49:20.166
[door closes]

49:22.376 --> 49:23.627
[sighs]

49:28.424 --> 49:30.468
I wonder what they're up to now.

49:31.302 --> 49:34.096
[♪ elegant classical music continuing]

49:38.601 --> 49:41.937
Sorry, I shouldn't have asked
what I did earlier.

49:42.021 --> 49:43.272
I'll take that back…

49:43.856 --> 49:46.066
-[groans softly, inhales sharply]
-[cutlery scraping]

49:46.150 --> 49:48.360
-Are you not feeling well?
-What?

49:50.988 --> 49:53.699
-[grunts]
-[high-pitched ringing]

49:53.782 --> 49:55.159
-[whooshes]
-[grunts softly]

49:55.242 --> 49:56.785
-[ice cubes crunch]
-[clattering]

49:56.869 --> 49:59.205
-[grunts softly]
-[clinking]

49:59.288 --> 50:00.581
[♪ tense music playing]

50:00.664 --> 50:01.665
-[glasses clink]
-[corks pop]

50:01.749 --> 50:03.250
[groans softly]

50:03.334 --> 50:04.460
Excuse me…

50:05.252 --> 50:06.670
-[server 1 yelps]
-[shatters]

50:08.589 --> 50:09.590
[gasps]

50:09.715 --> 50:11.008
[server 1 exclaims]

50:12.009 --> 50:13.844
I'm so sorry. I'll pay for all this.

50:13.928 --> 50:16.013
Can you put in the order again?
Just a moment, please.

50:16.597 --> 50:17.723
All right.

50:19.558 --> 50:21.769
[server 2] I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

50:23.479 --> 50:25.481
[♪ tense music continues]

50:27.358 --> 50:29.735
-[breathing heavily]
-[door opens, closes]

50:30.694 --> 50:32.655
Are you okay? Do you feel dizzy?

50:34.281 --> 50:35.699
[sighs] Is there a pharmacy nearby?

50:37.451 --> 50:41.038
I'm sorry.
I don't do well in noisy places.

50:41.705 --> 50:43.791
-Is it hard being around crowds?
-No.

50:45.251 --> 50:46.418
Mmm…

50:46.502 --> 50:48.128
[high-pitched ringing]

50:49.713 --> 50:51.131
[inhales deeply]

50:51.215 --> 50:53.926
-I can't hear… on this side.
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]

50:55.135 --> 50:57.137
I'm usually fine,

50:57.221 --> 50:59.932
but the sounds get mixed up
when it's noisy inside.

51:00.558 --> 51:02.643
And I can't even hear
the person right in front of me.

51:02.726 --> 51:05.563
It's hard to tell
the direction of the sounds.

51:07.147 --> 51:08.399
Excuse me.

51:08.482 --> 51:10.985
Excuse me! No, not that way…

51:11.068 --> 51:13.487
Can you hold it on the other side?

51:13.571 --> 51:15.698
[♪ soft emotional music continuing]

51:16.532 --> 51:19.243
But I'm a skilled artist, I'm friendly,

51:19.326 --> 51:21.412
and with my looks… [chuckles]

51:21.495 --> 51:22.580
What?

51:23.455 --> 51:26.917
I'm a really lucky guy besides the fact
that I can't hear on one side,

51:27.585 --> 51:29.753
so you don't have to look at me like that.

51:30.879 --> 51:32.298
[Chan inhales sharply]

51:32.381 --> 51:35.342
[sighs] I'll go deal
with the mess I caused in there.

51:35.968 --> 51:39.138
No, it's noisy in there.
I'll go bring our stuff.

51:43.684 --> 51:45.728
[door opens, closes]

51:45.811 --> 51:47.187
[inhales sharply]

51:47.271 --> 51:48.397
I…

51:49.189 --> 51:50.190
Hang on.

51:55.863 --> 51:57.948
Excuse me for a moment.

52:02.369 --> 52:04.371
[♪ tender song playing]

52:18.927 --> 52:22.556
I'm just taking care
of your ruined clothes, as a designer.

52:22.640 --> 52:24.683
It's not because I feel bad or anything.

52:25.267 --> 52:28.354
-Why are you drawing a line like that?
-Think however you want.

52:28.437 --> 52:29.438
Thank you.

52:33.609 --> 52:34.860
Thanks

52:36.028 --> 52:37.029
for caring.

52:45.412 --> 52:47.206
I took care of it for now.

52:47.289 --> 52:48.457
There.

52:48.540 --> 52:50.376
No, you'll catch a cold…

52:50.459 --> 52:52.169
It was just to style my outfit.

52:53.003 --> 52:55.673
I'll tell my grandmother
she had a misunderstanding.

52:55.756 --> 52:57.841
It's a good opportunity.
It's fine with me--

52:57.925 --> 53:00.386
I'm not fine with it.

53:01.053 --> 53:02.388
I don't like feeling indebted.

53:03.722 --> 53:05.599
Anyway, I'll bring our stuff.

53:13.565 --> 53:16.944
[Chan] How did you get close to Ms. Song?

53:17.569 --> 53:20.447
[Manjae] What? Well… [chuckles]

53:21.198 --> 53:24.910
I think we're close,
but I'm not sure about her.

53:25.619 --> 53:26.954
But why do you ask?

53:27.037 --> 53:28.122
Well…

53:29.248 --> 53:30.958
It feels like she always draws a line

53:31.625 --> 53:33.585
and doesn't let me cross it.

53:34.378 --> 53:36.004
She didn't use to…

53:38.340 --> 53:42.094
It just feels like it's hard
to get close to her. [chuckles]

53:42.177 --> 53:45.222
I've seen her every day
for the past seven years,

53:45.305 --> 53:48.517
but I had no idea what she did
or where she lived.

53:48.600 --> 53:50.519
She never talks about herself.

53:53.105 --> 53:55.858
-[♪ soft pleasant music playing]
-She was always drawing clothes,

53:56.400 --> 53:59.570
so I just assumed she was a designer.

54:00.487 --> 54:03.949
She always came by herself
and stayed here quietly.

54:04.032 --> 54:05.451
-[rain pattering]
-[Manjae exclaims]

54:06.118 --> 54:08.454
[Chan] Did she ever come with anyone else?

54:08.537 --> 54:09.830
[Manjae] No, never.

54:09.913 --> 54:11.457
Not once in seven years.

54:12.207 --> 54:14.126
She was always by herself.

54:14.960 --> 54:16.003
Always.

54:17.379 --> 54:20.883
[Haran sneezing]

54:20.966 --> 54:22.009
[sighs]

54:22.843 --> 54:24.803
Did you catch a cold?

54:24.887 --> 54:26.847
No, I was just sneezing.

54:26.930 --> 54:28.015
[sneezes]

54:29.391 --> 54:30.601
[Haran sighs]

54:32.978 --> 54:34.104
[sighs softly]

54:35.105 --> 54:37.816
-Huh? Where did it go?
-[♪ mysterious music playing]

54:43.280 --> 54:45.449
Gosh, you're stirring up dust.

54:45.532 --> 54:46.575
What are you doing?

54:46.658 --> 54:48.785
I can't find my drawing pen.

54:50.287 --> 54:51.497
Where did it go?

54:56.418 --> 54:58.629
Where are you going?
It's time for our meeting.

55:00.047 --> 55:01.256
[sighs]

55:03.175 --> 55:04.176
[sighs]

55:04.259 --> 55:06.428
[in English] I really liked
the, uh... the dancheong idea.

55:06.512 --> 55:08.805
So could you tell me
a little bit more about it?

55:08.889 --> 55:12.351
Of course.
Director Song will go over it for you.

55:12.434 --> 55:13.560
Director Song?

55:16.980 --> 55:19.525
[Hayeong coughing, speaking Korean]
The data overview.

55:20.817 --> 55:22.319
Oh, the data…

55:24.112 --> 55:27.449
[in English] Dancheong is
a traditional Korean coloring technique.

55:27.533 --> 55:28.534
[in Korean] Thank you.

55:28.617 --> 55:31.245
[Nana in English]
Commonly found in palaces and temples.

55:31.828 --> 55:35.624
It involves painting
wooden architecture with…

55:35.707 --> 55:39.086
Okay, so I'll see you at the next meeting.
We'll talk more about it then.

55:39.169 --> 55:40.379
All right. Bye-bye, everybody.

55:40.462 --> 55:41.505
[all] Bye!

55:41.588 --> 55:42.798
[Ben] See you.

55:44.132 --> 55:47.135
[Remy sighs, speaking Korean]
Great work, everyone.

55:48.554 --> 55:49.638
[clears throat]

55:52.391 --> 55:53.892
What kind of attitude was that?

55:55.143 --> 55:57.312
I'm sorry, but I have to go.

56:04.736 --> 56:06.113
[sighs]

56:06.905 --> 56:07.906
[sighs]

56:10.158 --> 56:12.661
[♪ pensive music playing]

56:14.413 --> 56:15.914
[gasping]

56:15.998 --> 56:17.207
Gosh. It's not here!

56:19.001 --> 56:21.587
Hang on. Where did I last use it?

56:22.379 --> 56:23.755
Right. The restaurant!

56:23.839 --> 56:25.841
[breathing heavily]

56:29.386 --> 56:30.679
The restaurant?

56:32.431 --> 56:34.266
NAUM LOST-AND-FOUND LIST

56:37.436 --> 56:39.313
We haven't found anything like that.

56:40.480 --> 56:42.274
Could I search for it myself?

56:42.357 --> 56:44.026
There are customers eating inside.

56:44.109 --> 56:47.404
But if you dropped it,
we would have found it while cleaning.

56:47.487 --> 56:48.572
[sighs]

56:49.239 --> 56:53.368
I'm really sorry,
but can I take a look after you're closed?

56:53.452 --> 56:55.412
Just for 30, no, 10 minutes.

56:55.495 --> 56:58.248
It's really valuable to me,
so I have to find it.

56:58.332 --> 56:59.583
Please.

56:59.666 --> 57:01.835
[♪ sentimental music playing]

57:01.918 --> 57:02.919
[Chan] No.

57:03.003 --> 57:05.255
You're going downtown later anyway.

57:05.339 --> 57:07.007
Just get me something I can gift.

57:07.090 --> 57:10.510
Anything that a woman
in her twenties can use.

57:10.594 --> 57:12.846
We're not close enough
to ask for favors like that.

57:13.388 --> 57:14.473
Do that for me, okay?

57:16.933 --> 57:19.603
-[door opens, closes]
-[sighs heavily]

57:25.108 --> 57:28.654
[shopkeeper in English] Is it a gift?
I could engrave it if you'd like.

57:28.737 --> 57:30.155
[sighs]

57:34.910 --> 57:36.370
[footsteps approaching]

57:36.453 --> 57:37.579
[sighs]

57:39.122 --> 57:40.248
[Chan sighs]

57:40.916 --> 57:41.917
Did you find it?

57:42.709 --> 57:44.211
I'll look for it after they close.

57:44.711 --> 57:45.837
I'm sure it'll be there.

57:46.463 --> 57:49.341
Let's go. We can stay at SHIM
and come back to look for it.

57:49.424 --> 57:52.594
No, this is a personal matter.
I can find it by myself.

57:53.220 --> 57:54.429
[coughs, sniffles]

58:02.562 --> 58:04.564
-Wear this for now.
-No…

58:04.648 --> 58:08.026
I'm just trying to help
with your coughing, as an animator.

58:08.735 --> 58:11.571
Plus, even if you dropped it here,
someone could have taken it.

58:13.657 --> 58:15.951
Anyway, let's go somewhere warm--

58:16.034 --> 58:17.035
I'll…

58:18.078 --> 58:19.579
deal with this by myself.

58:21.623 --> 58:23.083
Thanks for your concern,

58:23.834 --> 58:25.460
but leaving is helping me.

58:26.378 --> 58:27.838
[coughs, sniffles]

58:28.922 --> 58:30.716
What are you going to do, then?

58:30.799 --> 58:33.176
Wait out here
when you're coughing like this?

58:33.260 --> 58:34.720
It's just some pen.

58:35.846 --> 58:37.264
[scoffs]

58:37.347 --> 58:38.849
You don't know anything about it.

58:39.766 --> 58:43.562
I'm already upset
without you making it worse, so just…

58:44.730 --> 58:47.524
[sighing]

58:48.150 --> 58:50.861
[stutters] Where are you going?

58:50.944 --> 58:53.071
You won't leave me alone, so I'm leaving.

58:53.155 --> 58:57.492
It might be "just some pen,"
but I have to find it, no matter what.

58:57.576 --> 58:58.577
[grunts]

58:59.578 --> 59:00.787
Fine, I'll leave.

59:01.663 --> 59:03.331
-So wear this.
-Please, just…

59:03.415 --> 59:04.416
[Chan clears throat]

59:05.709 --> 59:06.752
Just take it.

59:07.294 --> 59:09.296
[♪ sentimental music continuing]

59:11.339 --> 59:12.340
[Haran sighs]

59:38.450 --> 59:39.868
"Just some pen."

59:40.619 --> 59:41.828
[sighs]

59:42.454 --> 59:44.247
I feel bad for saying that.

59:44.331 --> 59:45.624
Hey, roomie.

59:46.750 --> 59:48.543
-Yes.
-I'm sorry.

59:49.419 --> 59:52.172
Gosh. Sorry. [chuckles]

59:52.255 --> 59:53.507
Oh, my…

59:54.382 --> 59:56.968
You must have gone through
something awful.

59:57.052 --> 59:59.971
-You always seemed so cheerful.
-Oh…

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:02.557
[inhales sharply]
Do you want to try touching it?

01:00:02.641 --> 01:00:04.684
[chuckles] It doesn't hurt at all now.

01:00:04.768 --> 01:00:05.769
[scoffs]

01:00:06.269 --> 01:00:09.981
It seems you got something drawn
on your chest.

01:00:10.690 --> 01:00:12.192
[Chan] Ah. My tattoo?

01:00:12.275 --> 01:00:14.402
But why is it "memento mori"
of all phrases?

01:00:14.486 --> 01:00:17.572
It's like a warning to myself.

01:00:17.656 --> 01:00:19.866
-A warning?
-Yes.

01:00:20.659 --> 01:00:23.745
"You never know when you might die."

01:00:24.663 --> 01:00:28.083
"So live your life without regrets."

01:00:28.583 --> 01:00:29.960
Something like that. [chuckles]

01:00:30.919 --> 01:00:31.920
[inhales sharply]

01:00:32.712 --> 01:00:34.422
But what's that for?

01:00:34.506 --> 01:00:36.591
Didn't you just pick this up somewhere?

01:00:36.675 --> 01:00:38.343
Yes, it was snapped.

01:00:38.426 --> 01:00:39.594
[chuckles]

01:00:39.678 --> 01:00:42.013
Well, it grew roots.

01:00:42.097 --> 01:00:43.557
What?

01:00:44.516 --> 01:00:45.517
[exclaims, chuckles]

01:00:46.309 --> 01:00:48.728
I thought it would wither soon. [exclaims]

01:00:48.812 --> 01:00:51.231
I think it's time
to take it out of the glass.

01:00:52.107 --> 01:00:56.653
If I move it into a pot
and take good care of it, it'll grow well.

01:00:57.612 --> 01:00:58.738
[Manjae chuckles]

01:00:58.822 --> 01:01:00.824
Here you go.

01:01:08.123 --> 01:01:09.916
"Time to take it out"?

01:01:10.625 --> 01:01:13.003
By the way, roomie.

01:01:13.795 --> 01:01:18.049
-Yes?
-So, are you living without any regrets?

01:01:20.719 --> 01:01:23.013
[♪ sentimental song playing]

01:01:25.932 --> 01:01:28.977
Why would you do that?
If something happened to you…

01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:32.564
[Yujeong] Gosh.
You suddenly cut all contact with us.

01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:35.483
Sorry, Yujeong. I'm in a hurry right now.

01:01:36.484 --> 01:01:38.361
It's really valuable to me,
so I have to find it.

01:01:38.445 --> 01:01:41.323
It might be "just some pen,"
but I have to find it.

01:01:44.159 --> 01:01:46.786
[Manjae] I think it's time
to take it out of the glass.

01:01:46.870 --> 01:01:48.914
[♪ sentimental song continuing]

01:01:49.998 --> 01:01:50.999
[sighs]

01:01:53.877 --> 01:01:54.920
[door opens]

01:01:56.379 --> 01:01:58.006
[♪ sentimental song continues]

01:02:00.342 --> 01:02:02.218
-[cell phone beeps, dialing]
-[Haran] Chan, do you remember

01:02:02.928 --> 01:02:06.014
how I said I felt like
I was surrounded by walls?

01:02:06.598 --> 01:02:08.600
[vibrating]

01:02:13.146 --> 01:02:17.108
I suddenly found myself
unable to sketch anything,

01:02:17.192 --> 01:02:18.985
and I had no energy.

01:02:19.069 --> 01:02:20.904
I just wanted to give up on everything.

01:02:22.155 --> 01:02:24.032
[Chan panting]

01:02:28.495 --> 01:02:32.207
[Haran] But when I first held the pen
you gave to me for my birthday,

01:02:32.290 --> 01:02:34.834
I was suddenly able to draw something.

01:02:35.669 --> 01:02:37.921
And I won first place
in the contest with it.

01:02:39.255 --> 01:02:42.092
I would have run away
if I hadn't gotten such great results.

01:02:42.175 --> 01:02:43.510
Excuse me.

01:02:43.593 --> 01:02:45.553
[Haran] So you saved me.

01:02:46.763 --> 01:02:49.224
Thanks to you and this pen,

01:02:49.307 --> 01:02:51.768
I realized how much I love my job.

01:02:52.852 --> 01:02:55.313
It's a really precious pen to me.

01:02:55.397 --> 01:02:57.440
-"Haran" is engraved on the lid.
-Thank you.

01:02:57.524 --> 01:03:01.486
I'll draw lots of amazing clothes
and become a great designer.

01:03:01.569 --> 01:03:03.905
-[staff] Excuse me.
-[sighs]

01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:06.950
I'm sorry, but we have to go home now.

01:03:07.033 --> 01:03:08.868
[sighs] Right. I'm sorry.

01:03:08.952 --> 01:03:12.998
If you ever find it,
can you contact me through this number?

01:03:17.502 --> 01:03:21.798
[Manjae] So, are you living
without any regrets?

01:03:23.383 --> 01:03:24.551
[Chan] No.

01:03:24.634 --> 01:03:26.886
I think I'll have a lot of regrets later.

01:03:27.721 --> 01:03:30.348
[Manjae] Then what should you do
to not have regrets?

01:03:31.391 --> 01:03:34.269
[Chan] I want someone
to have joy in their life.

01:03:35.020 --> 01:03:37.188
Instead of their bleak life now,

01:03:37.272 --> 01:03:40.608
I want it to be vibrant, like before.

01:03:40.692 --> 01:03:43.194
I lived like that thanks to her.

01:03:43.987 --> 01:03:46.364
[Manjae] Then you can give her that joy.

01:03:46.448 --> 01:03:50.785
[Chan] I'd love to,
but I'm not sure if I have the right.

01:03:51.286 --> 01:03:56.207
[Manjae] I don't think you need rights
to want someone to be happy,

01:03:56.958 --> 01:04:00.211
as long as you're sincere about it.

01:04:00.295 --> 01:04:03.590
[cell phone vibrating]

01:04:09.345 --> 01:04:11.639
-Hello? Did you find--
-[Chan] You're still there, right?

01:04:11.723 --> 01:04:13.892
Are you there?
I have something to tell you.

01:04:13.975 --> 01:04:15.477
No, I'm…

01:04:15.560 --> 01:04:18.229
[Chan panting]

01:04:20.815 --> 01:04:22.609
I guess you haven't found it yet.

01:04:23.234 --> 01:04:24.486
Well…

01:04:24.569 --> 01:04:26.738
I'm sorry. I was rude earlier.

01:04:29.032 --> 01:04:30.492
Hang on…

01:04:30.575 --> 01:04:32.410
[panting]

01:04:32.494 --> 01:04:33.495
[exclaims]

01:04:35.872 --> 01:04:38.792
"Let's live so I won't have any regrets
when they close my coffin."

01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:42.337
That's my life motto.
But I thought I'd have regrets.

01:04:43.004 --> 01:04:45.465
That's why I came here.
I didn't want that to happen.

01:04:47.801 --> 01:04:51.763
I return to the US in three months,
and I probably won't come back to Korea.

01:04:51.846 --> 01:04:53.181
Why are you telling me this?

01:04:53.264 --> 01:04:56.142
I want to meddle in each other's affairs,
feel indebted,

01:04:56.226 --> 01:04:58.937
and have fun together with you, Ms. Song.

01:05:00.522 --> 01:05:01.856
What are you saying?

01:05:01.940 --> 01:05:04.275
Let's not think about the past or future.

01:05:04.984 --> 01:05:06.277
Let's just have fun

01:05:07.028 --> 01:05:08.530
until I head back.

01:05:08.613 --> 01:05:10.990
Just until next spring.

01:05:11.825 --> 01:05:13.952
Let's have fun like we're on a picnic.

01:05:14.035 --> 01:05:16.037
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:05:18.081 --> 01:05:20.917
[Manjae] But I'm really curious.

01:05:21.501 --> 01:05:25.505
Who is this person you want to be happy?

01:05:37.308 --> 01:05:38.518
[laptop pings]

01:05:39.811 --> 01:05:41.604
-[sighs]
-[laptop pings]

01:05:44.816 --> 01:05:46.776
[pinging continues]

01:05:46.860 --> 01:05:48.903
[pinging rapidly]

01:05:49.821 --> 01:05:51.489
[groaning]

01:05:51.573 --> 01:05:53.158
-I was trying to die…
-[groans]

01:05:53.741 --> 01:05:55.827
[EKG beeping]

01:05:56.411 --> 01:05:57.954
And I almost died.

01:05:59.164 --> 01:06:01.583
But she brought me back twice.

01:06:03.376 --> 01:06:05.086
A grateful disruption

01:06:06.087 --> 01:06:07.714
that made me live again.

01:06:10.800 --> 01:06:14.679
Is it okay if I start being
really nice to you from now on?

01:06:15.555 --> 01:06:17.724
[♪ upbeat love song playing]

01:06:29.027 --> 01:06:30.778
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:06:54.886 --> 01:06:57.430
[Haran] I don't think
we'll ever be friends.

01:06:57.513 --> 01:07:00.516
[Nana] Someone who's "talking" to a guy
is home at this hour?

01:07:00.600 --> 01:07:03.937
[Haran] I can't even go to the cafe
I love the most because of you!

01:07:04.020 --> 01:07:06.356
I don't need any new variables.

01:07:06.439 --> 01:07:10.902
[Manjae] A lot of them
just wither and die.

01:07:10.985 --> 01:07:15.573
[Chan] I'll move out
so we don't have to see each other again.

01:07:15.657 --> 01:07:19.869
I'll be gone
once our contract is over in three months.

01:07:19.953 --> 01:07:21.079
[Haran sighs]

01:07:21.162 --> 01:07:25.124
[Haran] I'd like to step away
from this collaboration project.

01:07:29.128 --> 01:07:31.130
[♪ theme music playing]

01:07:37.011 --> 01:07:38.012
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:07:38.096 --> 01:07:39.097
Translated by Juyoung Park
